# Xenomai 3 (Cobalt) Kernel for ARM64

This kernel tree has Xenomai 3 (Cobalt) real-time extension with Dovetail
interrupt pipeline integrated.

## Quick Start

### Prerequisites

- ARM64 cross compiler (aarch64-none-linux-gnu-)
- Standard Linux kernel build dependencies
- autoconf, automake and libtool (userspace libraries only)

### Build Kernel

```bash
# Using the build script
./build-kernel.sh

# Or manually
export CROSS_COMPILE=aarch64-none-linux-gnu-
export ARCH=arm64
rm -f .config .config.old
make LOCALVERSION= defconfig cix.config
./scripts/config --enable CONFIG_XENOMAI
./scripts/config --enable CONFIG_DOVETAIL
make LOCALVERSION= olddefconfig
make LOCALVERSION= -j$(nproc) Image modules dtbs
make LOCALVERSION= bindeb-pkg  # For DEB packages
```

`LOCALVERSION=` is passed empty so that `scripts/setlocalversion` does not
append a `+` to the release string; the suffix itself comes from
`CONFIG_LOCALVERSION` in `cix.config`.

The script will generate DEB packages under `../xenomai3-out/debs/` (relative to kernel source):
- `linux-image-*.deb` - Kernel image
- `linux-headers-*.deb` - Kernel headers
- `linux-libc-dev_*.deb` - Kernel libc development files

### Build Userspace Libraries (libcobalt)

```bash
# Using the build script (automatically clones Xenomai 3)
./build-userspace.sh

# The Xenomai 3 source will be cloned to ../xenomai3-src/ (relative to kernel dir)
# DEB package will be generated at ../xenomai3-out/debs/cix-libcobalt-xenomai3_*.deb
```

### Configuration

`cix.config` sets the kernel version suffix:

- `CONFIG_LOCALVERSION="-cix-build-xenomai3"` - Kernel version suffix

Cobalt is enabled by the `XENOMAI` Kconfig default in `init/Kconfig`, which
also selects `DOVETAIL`, so `make defconfig cix.config` already yields
`CONFIG_XENOMAI=y` and `CONFIG_DOVETAIL=y`. The `scripts/config --enable`
calls above re-assert both, as `build-kernel.sh` does, so that a changed
default cannot silently drop them.

### Install

```bash
# Install kernel packages on target
dpkg -i linux-image-*.deb linux-headers-*.deb linux-libc-dev_*.deb

# Install Xenomai userspace libraries
dpkg -i cix-libcobalt-xenomai3_*.deb
```

The Xenomai userspace will be installed under `/usr/xenomai/`:
- Libraries: `/usr/xenomai/lib/`
- Headers: `/usr/xenomai/include/`
- Tools: `/usr/xenomai/bin/`

---

*Standard Linux kernel README follows below*
---

Linux kernel
============

There are several guides for kernel developers and users. These guides can
be rendered in a number of formats, like HTML and PDF. Please read
Documentation/admin-guide/README.rst first.

In order to build the documentation, use ``make htmldocs`` or
``make pdfdocs``.  The formatted documentation can also be read online at:

    https://www.kernel.org/doc/html/latest/

There are various text files in the Documentation/ subdirectory,
several of them using the Restructured Text markup notation.

Please read the Documentation/process/changes.rst file, as it contains the
requirements for building and running the kernel, and information about
the problems which may result by upgrading your kernel.
